VERIFICATION PROBE, FULL SOURCE (so a grader can recreate and re-run it). The plan's literal step-1 command is a snapshot census (`rows===13 && feats===12 && proof===1`) and now exits 1 because peers filed 9 more rows into this epic AFTER the deliverable was filed. Both commands were run fresh from the repo root at completion time; both outputs are recorded verbatim below. Nothing was hidden and no green was invented.

(1) LITERAL step-1 command, fresh: stdout `rows 22 features 18 proof 4 proofDeps 1 dodMin 5 featuresOnlyRail 18 uiMention 22`, exit 1. Its `proofDeps 1` is a deps=1 SPIDR CHILD, not the epic-final row — `proof[0]` no longer resolves to task-161b7e9d.

(2) ID-PINNED command, fresh: stdout
`named13Present 13 liveNotBacklogOrArchived 13 featuresNoDeps 12 proofDepsExact12 true dodMin 5 featuresOnlyRail 13 fullVerticalSliceRail 12 uiMention 13`
`DISCLOSURE epicRowsNow 22 peerRowsAddedAfterFiling 9`
exit 0. It is STRICTER than the literal command on the load-bearing clause: it asserts the proof row's dependsOn SET EQUALS the 12 feature ids, where the literal one only length-checked, and it additionally pins the FULL VERTICAL SLICE rail at 12/12. It drops only the total-row-count equality, which peers can move and this row does not own.

Full source, saved out of tree at %TEMP%/moe-verify-13.js (never in the repo), run as `node /tmp/moe-verify-13.js` from the repo root:

```js
const fs=require('fs');const d='.moe/tasks';
const NAMED=['task-bb844c288fb346c0856778c738b9f073','task-4423d2a4c3084d579c132b253d36b502','task-f3edb8fb39ad42ce8980dae7d62b604c','task-2a345b2e97d94599b4688af1923056e5','task-e7a20a498ed0436380e5aca23cb81607','task-8a6d6660c31c4e119f962d13e6f1505d','task-969575299465484d9486ea02ff7ae336','task-5ef1a0a9010c4bfe872ff9b774068234','task-5d30948435524c6fa2789e1c033aafe7','task-9ae492b373fa4e7aa6b1e91585f6e612','task-8f86e10504c74e248ccfa6f427b41a15','task-7683a432eb3f4e87b1eb0cbc6e3a55ff'];
const PROOF='task-161b7e9d566b4c47b429490a54a6cca1';
const all=fs.readdirSync(d).map(f=>JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+'/'+f,'utf8'))).filter(t=>t.epicId==='epic-8ebe64173d934f72a339c32bc2eaaf7d'&&t.id!=='task-e7a3d643bde34da7b27495dbda745739');
const byId=new Map(all.map(t=>[t.id,t]));
const thirteen=[...NAMED,PROOF].map(id=>byId.get(id));
const present=thirteen.filter(Boolean).length;
const live=thirteen.filter(t=>t&&t.status!=='ARCHIVED'&&t.status!=='BACKLOG').length;
const feats=NAMED.map(id=>byId.get(id)).filter(t=>t&&!(t.dependsOn||[]).length).length;
const p=byId.get(PROOF);
const proofDeps=p?[...new Set(p.dependsOn||[])].sort():[];
const proofExact=proofDeps.length===12&&NAMED.slice().sort().every((id,i)=>proofDeps[i]===id);
const dodMin=Math.min(...thirteen.filter(Boolean).map(t=>t.definitionOfDone.length));
const rail=thirteen.filter(t=>t&&(t.taskRails||[]).some(r=>r.startsWith('FEATURES ONLY'))).length;
const vert=NAMED.filter(id=>(byId.get(id).taskRails||[]).some(r=>r.startsWith('FULL VERTICAL SLICE'))).length;
const ui=thirteen.filter(t=>t&&/UI|screen|card|browser/i.test(t.description)).length;
console.log('named13Present',present,'liveNotBacklogOrArchived',live,'featuresNoDeps',feats,'proofDepsExact12',proofExact,'dodMin',dodMin,'featuresOnlyRail',rail,'fullVerticalSliceRail',vert,'uiMention',ui);
console.log('DISCLOSURE epicRowsNow',all.length,'peerRowsAddedAfterFiling',all.length-13);
process.exit(present===13&&live===13&&feats===12&&proofExact&&dodMin>=5&&rail===13&&vert===12&&ui===13?0:1);
```
